<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions six-month bonds in special OMO.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions six-month bonds in special OMO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan auctioned short-term federal bonds worth a total of 200 million rupees in a special open market operation on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bank said bids worth 200 million rupees had been submitted for the outright sale of the bonds and all had been accepted at a maximum cutt-off rate of 15.1 percent a year.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
